  <h1>Know the four signs of type 1 diabetes</h1>
  <p class="lede">Type 1 can start at any age and come on over a few weeks. In young children it can be much faster.</p>

  <ul class="ts">
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 60 60" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="30" cy="30" r="30" fill="#EEF3FF"/><rect x="20" y="12" width="20" height="36" rx="3" fill="#fff" stroke="#1B2430" stroke-width="2.5"/><rect x="24" y="16" width="12" height="13" rx="2" fill="#F2A93B"/><circle cx="25" cy="35" r="2" fill="#1B2430"/></svg>
      <div><b>Toilet</b><span>Peeing a lot, getting up in the night, or bedwetting in a child who was dry.</span></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 60 60" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="30" cy="30" r="30" fill="#EEF3FF"/><path d="M19 14h22l-3 32H22Z" fill="#fff" stroke="#1B2430" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M20.5 30h19L38 45H22Z" fill="#9FB4FF"/></svg>
      <div><b>Thirsty</b><span>A thirst that drinking doesn't fix.</span></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 60 60" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="30" cy="30" r="30" fill="#EEF3FF"/><text x="16" y="44" font-family="Bricolage Grotesque, sans-serif" font-weight="800" font-size="30" fill="#1B2430">z</text><text x="34" y="27" font-family="Bricolage Grotesque, sans-serif" font-weight="800" font-size="20" fill="#F2A93B">z</text></svg>
      <div><b>Tired</b><span>Wiped out for no reason, with no energy for normal things.</span></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 60 60" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="30" cy="30" r="30" fill="#EEF3FF"/><rect x="8" y="23" width="44" height="14" rx="3" fill="#8A5A1F"/><rect x="21" y="17" width="20" height="26" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="#1B2430" stroke-width="3.5"/><line x1="24" y1="30" x2="42" y2="30" stroke="#1B2430" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      <div><b>Thinner</b><span>Losing weight without trying.</span></div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="act">Seen any of these? Ask a doctor for a test today.<small>You don't need all four signs. A quick finger-prick or urine test is the first check. If it shows high sugar, a hospital confirms it with more blood tests.</small></p>

  <p class="urgent"><b>Go to emergency care now if they also</b><span>are being sick, have tummy pain, are breathing fast and deep, have breath that smells fruity, or are very sleepy or confused.</span></p>

